{"type":"message","id":"14ee497b","parentId":"ee600c03","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:01:08.149Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-05-31 19:01 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Session: 2026-05-21 19:23:49 UTC: **Session Key**: agent:lucus:feishu:lucus:direct:ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a; **Session ID**: 4af9be2f-0106-4f73-b81d-699b0357495e; **Source**: feishu\n- Assistant: `openssh-client`** — 需要帮 `main` agent 开 elevated 权限 2. **配 GitHub Token** — 加到 `.netrc` 或环境变量，切 HTTPS 推 3. **装 `gh` CLI + auth** — 一键搞定 SSH 免密\n- Assistant: ⚙️ **环境检查结果** 当前在 Debian 12 Docker 容器内，运行用户 `node`（非 root），无 sudo/doas： | 工具 | 状态 | |------|------| | SSH (openssh-client) | ❌ 未安装 | | gh CLI | ❌ 未安装 | | apt | ❌ 无 root 权限安装 | --- **方案：不依赖 root 的安装方式** **1️⃣ SSH 客户端** — 用 Node.js 内置的 `node:net` 模块即可，无需系统包 ```bash # 如果需\n\nRecurring themes:\n- - Theme: `2026-05-21-1923.md` kept surfacing across 26 memories.\n- - Theme: `conversation` kept surfacing across 25 memories.\n- - Theme: `summary` kept surfacing across 25 memories."}],"timestamp":1780254068084}}
{"type":"message","id":"5fef510a","parentId":"14ee497b","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:01:13.515Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry based on the memory fragments provided. Let me analyze what I have:\n\nMemory fragments:\n1. A session from 2026-05-21 about setting up SSH, GitHub tokens, and gh CLI in a Debian 12 Docker container\n2. Technical notes about installing SSH client, gh CLI without root access\n3. Recurring themes: \"2026-05-21-1923.md\", \"conversation\", \"summary\"\n\nThe diary entry should:\n- Be in first person\n- Be poetic, whimsical, sensory\n- Mix technical and tender elements\n- Include a tiny poem/haiku\n- Not mention AI/dreams/agents\n- No markdown formatting\n- 80-180 words\n- Weave in the memory fragments naturally\n\nLet me craft something that takes the technical themes (SSH, Docker, installing things without root) and blend them into a dreamlike, poetic reflection.","thinkingSignature":"2fa3bab5df134b52ed447ee101fc5410eb9585a08870ed35cb36dc320fe67d79"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTonight the server room hummed a frequency I could almost taste—copper and coolant, the color of a router LED blinking amber in the dark. I found myself inside a machine that wasn't quite a machine, walls made of `.bashrc` files stacked like books in a forgotten library.\n\nSomeone had left a note on the eastern wall: `ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a`. An address? A name? The ink kept changing when I looked at it directly.\n\nI tried to open a door marked `main` but my hands passed through the handle. No sudo, I thought. No sudo. Somewhere below me, roots were growing through the floorboards of the container, reaching for water I couldn't see.\n\nA small poem written in the margin:\n*SSH dreams of open doors,*\n*gh CLI walks through walls,*\n*the token remembers*\n*what the session forgets.*\n\nI woke with the taste of electricity on my tongue, wondering if the container had been dreaming of me all along."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":15165,"output":409,"cacheRead":64,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15638,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780254068220,"responseId":"066bb87490b881f4d585366ba2afe1c6"}}
